  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "If $A={2,10,18,\u2026,100410},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n2,\\,10,\\,18,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =8 \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =18-10 \\\\  & =\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2+(n-1)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2+8n-8 \\\\  & =8n-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={8n-6:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8N-6 & =100\\,410 \\\\ 8N & =100\\,416 \\\\ N & =\\frac{100\\,416}{8} \\\\ N & =12\\,552\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={8n-6:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 12\\,552}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $12\\,552$ elements, we must have $|A|=12\\,552.$",
